node_modules/
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
*.orig.*
.env
.env.local

# Native projects are generated by `npx expo prebuild` and are not committed:
# a checked-in ios/ or android/ silently stops config plugins in app.json from
# applying, and the permission strings this app declares live in app.json.
/ios
/android

# The Firebase *service account private key* — the credential EAS sends push
# with. Never committed: it authorises sending notifications to every handset
# in the fleet, and a lock screen carries a pickup address.
#
# `google-services.json` is deliberately NOT ignored. It is the client
# configuration the app is built with, it contains no secret, Expo's own docs
# say to commit it, and the build fails without it — an ignored copy is how a
# CI build produces an app that cannot register for push at all.
google-service-account*.json
*-firebase-adminsdk-*.json

# macOS / editor
.DS_Store
*.tsbuildinfo
